{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369@rel:R19-11#bd580f6d","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R19-11","content":"Service Name Pdu R_<User:Lo>Trigger Transmit Syntax Std_ Return Type Pdu R_<User:Lo>Trigger Transmit ( Pdu Id Type Tx Pdu Id, Pdu Info Type* Pdu Info Ptr ) Service ID [hex] 0x41 Sync/ Async Synchronous Reentrancy Reentrant for different Pdu Ids. Non reentrant for the same Pdu Id. Parameters (in) Tx Pdu Id ID of the SDU that is requested to be transmitted. Parameters (inout) Pdu Info Ptr Contains a pointer to a buffer (Sdu Data Ptr) to where the SDU data shall be copied, and the available buffer size in Sdu Lengh. On return, the service will indicate the length of the copied SDU data in Sdu Length. Parameters (out) None Return value Std _ - Return - Type E_ OK: SDU has been copied and Sdu Length indicates the number of copied bytes. E_ NOT_ OK: No SDU data has been copied. Pdu Info Ptr must not be Specification of PDU Router AUTOSAR CP R19 - 11 71 of 130 Document ID 35 : AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter - AUTOSAR confidential - used since it may contain a NULL pointer or point to invalid data. Descr iption Within this API, the upper layer module (called module) shall check whether the available data fits into the buffer size reported by Pdu Info Ptr - >Sdu Length. If it fits, it shall copy its data into the buffer provided by Pdu Info Ptr - >Sdu Data Ptr and update the length of the actual copied data in Pdu Info Ptr - >Sdu Length. If not, it returns E_ NOT_ OK without changing Pdu Info Ptr. Available via Pdu R_<module>.h","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:13+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369@rel:R20-11#5331bd14","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R20-11","content":"67 of 125 Document ID 35: AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter Specification of PDU Router AUTOSAR CP R20-11 Service Name PduR_<User:Lo>TriggerTransmit Syntax Std_ReturnType PduR_<User : Lo>TriggerTransmit ( PduIdType TxPduId, PduInfoType * PduInfoPtr ) Service ID [hex] 0x41 Sync/Async Synchronous Reentrancy Reentrant for different PduIds. Non reentrant for the same PduId. Parameters (in) TxPduId ID of the SDU that is requested to be transmitted. Parameters (inout) PduInfoPtr Contains a pointer to a buffer (SduDataPtr) to where the SDU data shall be copied, and the available buffer size in SduLengh. On return, the service will indicate the length of the copied SDU data in SduLength. Parameters (out) None Return value Std_ReturnType E_OK: SDU has been copied and SduLength indicates the number of copied bytes. E_NOT_OK: No SDU data has been copied. PduInfoPtr must not be used since it may contain a NULL pointer or point to invalid data. Description Within this API, the upper layer module (called module) shall check whether the available data fits into the buffer size reported by PduInfoPtr->SduLength. If it fits, it shall copy its data into the buffer provided by PduInfoPtr->SduDataPtr and update the length of the actual copied data in PduInfoPtr->SduLength. If not, it returns E_NOT_OK without changing PduInfoPtr. Available via PduR_<module>.h","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:33+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369@rel:R21-11#f72526c3","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R21-11","content":"Service Name PduR_<User:Lo>TriggerTransmit Syntax Std_ReturnType PduR_<User : Lo>TriggerTransmit ( PduIdType TxPduId, PduInfoType * PduInfoPtr ) Service ID [hex] 0x41 Sync/Async Synchronous Reentrancy Reentrant for different PduIds. Non reentrant for the same PduId. 5 76 of 132 Document ID 35: AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter Specification of PDU Router AUTOSAR CP R21-11 4 Parameters (in) TxPduId ID of the SDU that is requested to be transmitted. Parameters (inout) PduInfoPtr Contains a pointer to a buffer (SduDataPtr) to where the SDU data shall be copied, and the available buffer size in SduLengh. On return, the service will indicate the length of the copied SDU data in SduLength. Parameters (out) None Return value Std_ReturnType E_OK: SDU has been copied and SduLength indicates the number of copied bytes. E_NOT_OK: No SDU data has been copied. PduInfoPtr must not be used since it may contain a NULL pointer or point to invalid data. Description Within this API, the upper layer module (called module) shall check whether the available data fits into the buffer size reported by PduInfoPtr->SduLength. If it fits, it shall copy its data into the buffer provided by PduInfoPtr->SduDataPtr and update the length of the actual copied data in PduInfoPtr->SduLength. If not, it returns E_NOT_OK without changing PduInfoPtr. Available via PduR_<module>.h","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_PDURouter.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:56+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","release":"R25-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_PduR_00369","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"lat